! mcp_bootstrap_p256.strap -- MCP printed page 256: the Input Program's
! card/tape recovery section, continued (CB+,VP,VRJTP .. ,($14)), with
! the operator message texts RKMSGE, RSMGSP, RDLEOF and the CCWs
! RECCW / RDCCW, lines 1-56.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.7, read at 400 dpi.  Header, READ:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID 0B000458  DIST. OF 3/01
! 3/01  PAGE NUMBER 256" (round glyphs in numeric fields read 0); the
! heading row's LOCATION field is 230354, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  56 lines; every line except 33 (a CNOP that pads nothing)
! is located, contiguous from 230354.00 to 230431.40 (a half word; next
! location 230432.00, which is RBSWRT, p.257 line 1 by the volume OCR).
! The landed/scratch neighbours agree on the join: p.245 SYNs RKSCON at
! 230355.0 = line 3 here.  Every line number prints with a trailing
! "*"; asterisks after the LOCATION on lines 4, 17, 20, 32 and 46.  No
! remarks.
!
! DATA TEXTS, character positions measured on a 40.08 px (400 dpi) grid
! anchored on each statement's "(":
!   * line 16 RKMSGE: 9 blanks, "EPGK", 3 blanks, "RESTART VIA IPL", 1
!     blank, then the "*" terminator = 32 characters = 4 words, matching
!     230365.00 -> 230371.00.
!   * line 21: 1 blank, "UNLOADING,REUSE TAPE", 3 blanks = 24 characters
!     = 3 words, 230375.00 -> 230400.00.  Printed "UNLCADING" (open O;
!     the English word is UNLOADING).
!   * line 32 RSMGSP: 1 blank, "STRIP", 11 blanks, "BEFORE REUSING", 1
!     blank = 32 characters = 4 words, 230405.00 -> 230411.00; line 33's
!     CNOP pads nothing and prints no location.
!   * line 34 RDLEOF (CC*)DD(BU,,12): "B", 8 blanks, "COMD,OFFLINE," =
!     22 twelve-bit characters = 264 bits; 230411.00 + 264 = 230415.10,
!     and line 35's half-word LX lands at 230415.40 as printed.  ("COMD"
!     as printed: the fourth glyph has the D's straight stem.)
!
! >>> LINE 34'S (CC*)DD IS ASSEMBLED (2026-11-10). <<<  It used to be
! a comment behind two stand-ins (RDLEOF SYN and SLC,(8)230415.40)
! while strap_asm refused entry mode CC.  Both assemblers now convert CC
! (C28-6129 p.16: each character its card column's punches, App. F
! p.56; the bit order row 12 high is
! ATBL's, printed p.331).  Unlike the PUNFUL header
! cards of pp.2, 15, 99 and 320-381, THIS ONE IS LOADED: no PUNFUL is in
! force, so its 264 bits are in the MCP image at 230411.00-230415.10
! (they were zeros before).  The 22 characters are MEASURED in the ink
! (PDF 7 at 300 dpi, the print's fixed pitch of 30 px per cell): "B" in
! cell 16, cells 17-24 blank, "COMD,OFFLINE," in 25-37, the "*" in 38.
! Line 35's printed 230415.40 allows 21-24 characters; the ink says 22.
! It is a card image of the operator command "COMD,OFFLINE," (B in
! column 1, the statement from column 10: C22-6678-1 pp.7-10).
! tests/check_strap2_punch.py A8 reads it back out of strap_asm's image.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * lines 4, 23 ",DICDEF" = DIODEF (open O): landed p.105/p.179
!     "DIODEF SYN,13.0"; prints 000015.00.
!   * lines 8, 27 ",DCCMM" = DCOMM: landed p.105 "D COMM SYN,35.32";
!     prints 000043.40.
!   * line 13 label RKSUB, line 3 RKSCON, line 14 RKSBRC, line 15 REJJOB
!     (printed "REJJCB"), line 18 RENXSC, line 12 RVSET3, line 22 REDUMP,
!     line 35 RPQUES (printed "RPCUES"): spellings as the landed/scratch
!     decks p.242-p.246 already SYN them, at these addresses.
!   * line 19 RDCCW (printed "RCCCW"-like, worn D stem): p.249 SYNs RDCCW
!     at 230373.0 = this row.
!   * line 34 label printed "RDLECF" = RDLEOF (open O; Read-EOF, cf.
!     p.249's REOF).  No deck spells it otherwise; nothing on this page
!     references it -- READ ON INK AND SENSE ONLY.
!   * line 17 label RECCW: as printed (C C W, cf. RDCCW, RRCCW).  Nothing
!     here references it.
!   * line 41 "SVA,$14,RWTRY": landed p.244 label RWTRY at 227643.40;
!     prints 227643.75 (the volume OCR reads it "RWIRY").
!   * line 47 "SIC,RBSWRT": T is clear in the 400 dpi ink; p.257 line 1
!     label "RBSWRT B," by the volume OCR at 230432.10's word.
!   * line 18 "B,RKS111": digits, as the family RKS112/RKS113/RKS114 in
!     the volume OCR of p.253.
!   * line 30 "B,REDMP" (not REDUMP, line 22's label at 230400.00):
!     prints 230346.10 = landed p.219's REDMP SYN at 230346.0.
!   * line 45 "CM0000(BU,1)": zeros, as the connective's four truth-
!     table digits (cf. p.164's CM1111).
!   * line 54 ",DCHEX" (worn H crossbar): landed p.104, 000014.00.
!   * lines 42, 46, 52 "-1.C" = -1.0; line 14 "BE,C.O" = BE,0.0; line 17
!     "XW,C.0" = XW,0.0: round glyphs in numeric literals.
!   * hex bytes printed with an open round written 0 ("C0" lines 2, 7,
!     13, 22, 26, 30, 48, 53; "C1" line 40 = 01).  Line 37 BZXE and line
!     44 BZXE print "C0" and ARE C0 (the BZXE opcode byte, as p.249 line
!     27).  "D0" lines 39, 41 (SVA) as printed; line 56 "8E" read at 900 dpi
!     (the E's bottom bar is faint at 400 dpi and reads F; the
!     statement's ($14) = E agrees).
!
! EXTERNALS FROM THIS PAGE'S BINARY ONLY (no landed definer):
!   RKNEG 230235.0 (B line 13 .10; volume OCR p.253 "RKNEG LVNI"),
!   RKS111 230240.40 (B line 18 .50), RKSTOT 230442.40 (BZXE line 37
!   .72, as $+1.32 on line 44 prints .72 for 230423.40), RECDMP 230341.0
!   (B line 50 .10; volume OCR p.255 "RECDMP S?C,RKCRWT", a half word),
!   RBSWRT 230432.0 (SIC line 47).  All half word only.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials run 0B000458 .. 0B000491 (prefix
! glyph round, as in the header).  Shared: 1-2 (458), 3-6 (459), 7-10
! (460), 22-25 (472), 26-29 (473), 35-37 (479), 38-39 (480), 40-41
! (481), 42-43 (482), 47-48 (486), 53-56 (491); every other line its
! own card.  No serial skipped; p.257 opens at 0B000492 (volume OCR).

DMCP    SYN, 32.0                    ! landed p.108 "D MCP SYN,32.0"; B lines 3, 7, 22, 26, 53
DIODEF  SYN, 13.0                    ! landed p.105/p.179; lines 4, 23 (printed "DICDEF")
DCOMM   SYN, 35.32                   ! landed p.105 line 23; lines 8, 27 (printed "DCCMM")
DCHEX   SYN, 12.0                    ! landed p.104 "D CHEX"; line 54 000014.00
